// Title: PUA - DIT Snapshot Viewer
// Sigma ID: d3b70aad-097e-409c-9df2-450f80dc476b
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Furkan Caliskan (@caliskanfurkan_)
// Date: 2020-07-04 | Modified: 2023-02-21
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.003
// Description: Detects the use of Ditsnap tool, an inspection tool for Active Directory database, ntds.dit.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate admin usage
// References:
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2020/06/21/snatch-ransomware/
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20201124182207/https://github.com/yosqueoy/ditsnap
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pua_ditsnap.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\ditsnap.exe" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ditsnap.exe"
